{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n2le03ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n2le03ob01re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n2le03ob01re2img01.jpg", "text": "<strong>Alex</strong>: That's it, I think my whole weekend is ruined!<br/>\n<strong>Jane</strong>: What is it? You look very concerned.<br/>\n<strong>Alex</strong>: Well, I am trying to write a subroutine, but it is taking too long. I guess I am working all weekend until I finish it.<br/>\n<strong>Jane</strong>: Let me take a look. Is that the subroutine?<br/>\n<strong>Alex</strong>: Yes, I am writing line after line of code, but apparently, it takes forever.<br/>\n<strong>Jane</strong>: I think I know how to save your weekend. I guess you don't know about automatic programming.<br/>\n<strong>Alex</strong>: What is automatic programming?", "time": "0"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n2le03ob01re2img02.jpg", "text": "<strong>Jane</strong>: Automatic programming is a tool that software developers use in order to facilitate their work by writing codes that are able to write other codes.<br/>\n<strong>Alex</strong>: I don't understand, is this some kind of magic?<br/>\n<strong>Jane</strong>: Not really. Automatic programming is a method of computer coding in which software programmers write high-level applications that in turn generate software code based on artificial specifications.<br/>\n<strong>Alex</strong>: That sounds fantastic! Are these specifications defined automatically?<br/>\n<strong>Jane</strong>: No, the programmer specifies the automatic coding parameters. There are two types of automatic programming. First, we have generative programming that uses standard logical libraries. Second, we find source code generation, which uses models or templates based on mathematical algorithms.", "time": "33000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n2le03ob01re2img03.jpg", "text": "<strong>Alex</strong>: I am using automatic programming to solve the subroutine. I am saving a lot of time. Finally, Jane, do you know how I can express these algorithms? They are recurrent in the entire program.<br/>\n<strong>Jane</strong>: Are those repeated over and over?<br/>\n<strong>Alex</strong>: Sure!<br/>\n<strong>Jane</strong>: You can use a programming idiom to do it. Programming idioms are expressions used for performing not only recurrent tasks but also for more complex algorithms, and even full data structures or patterns.<br/>\n<strong>Alex</strong>: Thanks, Jane. You are very helpful.", "time": "92000"}]}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about automatic programming.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can give information about automatic programming.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can explain what automatic programming is and some related facts.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What are the benefits of working with \"programmer friendly\" languages?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Why do you think that the syntax of some programming languages is similiar to the human language?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "A Tool That Makes a Programmer's Job Easier\t", "type": "fre