 "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations. Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Demonstrative Pronouns in Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <strong>demonstrative pronouns</strong> to replace a noun. We can use demonstrative pronouns in questions, and it is important that the noun we replaced for the demonstrative pronoun is clear for our interlocutor. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<strong>Demonstrative pronouns</strong> are words we use to point at something specific inside a sentence. They can be singular or plural, and refer to objects close or far in space or time.<br/><br/>  There are four demonstrative pronouns: <span class=\"italic\">this, these, that and those.</span><br/><br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Close in space and time</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Far in space and time</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><strong>Singular</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">This</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">That</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><strong>Plural</strong></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">These</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Those</div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Is that the subroutine?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Is this some kind of magic?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Are these specifications defined automatically?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Are those repeated over and over?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Examples: <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">This</span> is the new script for the application. <br/>                     He is correcting <span class=\"strong\">these</span> code errors. <br/>                     <span class=\"strong\">That</span> software was not ideal for our needs. <br/>                     <span class=\"strong\">Those</span> are the corrections that Sharon wrote. </span> <br/> <br/>   <span class=\"strong\">Demonstrative pronouns for asking questions</span>:<br/>   Before you use demonstrative pronouns to ask questions, t is very important that the person we are talking to knows in advance the thing or things the demonstrative pronoun is replacing. <br/>  <br/>    Grammatical structure: <br/>    <div class=\"center_text\"> <span class=\"strong\">Auxiliary verb</span> + <span class=\"strong\">demonstrative pronoun</span> + complement +?</div><br/>   Example: <span class=\"italic\">  <span class=\"strong\"> Are those</span> programs safe? <br/>   <span class=\"strong\"> Do these</span> programs offer everything we need? </span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adjectives Used to Describe Automatic Programming", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Automatic programming is a tool that software developers use in order to facilitate their work. You can use some specific <b>adjectives</b> to describe automatic programming e.g. high-level, artificial, mathematical, logical, etc.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"High-level\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Something very detailed, with a strong level of complexity. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Low-level\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Something not very detailed, with a mild level of complexity.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Artificial\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Something that humans created. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Mathematical\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Something exact, precise, and related to mathematics. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Logical\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Something that follows the principles of logic. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<div align=\"justify\">Let's see those <b>adjectives</b> in the next text:<br/><br/>  Automatic programming is a method of computer coding in which software programmers write <strong>high-level</strong> applications that in turn generate software code based on <strong>artificial</strong> specifications. In some way, translators are automatic programs that use a <strong>high-level</strong> language that they translate into a <strong>lower-level</strong> language, which is the specification.<br/><br/>  There are two types of automatic programming. First, we have generative programming that uses standard <strong>logical</strong> libraries for improving programming speed and efficiency. This process saves time since the programmer doesn't need to re-implement certain automatic elements during compile. Second, we find source code generation, which uses models or templates based on <strong>mathematical</strong> algorithms. Once the model is created, a source code generator creates the code based on how the components connect to each other in the resulting program. Automatic programming is also referred to as metaprogramming. </div>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Automatic programming is a method of computer coding in which software programmers write high-level applications that in turn generate software code based on artificial specifications.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We find source code generation, which uses models or templates based on mathematical algorithms.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "What does programming idiom mean?", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Similar to natural language, programming languages have expressions that we often repeat. We can use those expressions in certain circumstances.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We use a programming idiom when we want to express a recurrent concept in one or several programming languages. In general, a programming idiom is a way of expressing a repeated task that is a feature normally incorporated in the programming language that we are using. Programming idioms can even be present in different languages and have equivalent expressions and effects.<br/><br/>  Programming idioms are expressions used for performing not only recurrent tasks, but also more complex algorithms, and even full data structures or patterns.<br/><br/>  Like learning a natural language, remembering the idioms associated with a programming language, and how to use them in the appropriate context, is an important part of gaining fluency in that language. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "concerned", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be worried or upset", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What is it? You look very concerned.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "facilitate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a task easier  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Automatic programming is a tool that software developers use in order to facilitate their work. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "automatically ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "performed without human intervention  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are these specifications defined automatically? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "template ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that works as pattern for creation  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Second, we find source code generation, which uses models or templates based on mathematical algorithms. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "generative ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having the ability to originate or reproduce  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: First, we have generative programming that uses standard logical libraries to produce code. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "specify ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to mention clearly and precisely  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The programmer specifies the automatic coding parameters. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le03ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for information about automatic programming.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "List the most remarkable characteristics about it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a poster in which you present these characteristics.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present and discuss your points with your classmates.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I  find information about automatic programming.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can list the characteristics of automatic programing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can present and discuss automatic programming.", "type": "text"}]}]}